---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WorkCard from '../components/WorkCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const work = (await getCollection('work'))
  .filter((e) => e.data.pillars.includes('ai'))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
---
<Base
  title="Applied AI & teaching — Jai Kharbanda"
  description="Multi-week Claude Code curricula, live workshops where every attendee ships something, and the agent systems I build and run myself."
  active="ai"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Applied AI &amp; teaching</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      My rule for every session: the audience ships something before they leave. Slides are for
      context. The point is a working artefact, made by the attendee, live by the end.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Teaching</h2>
    <p>
      I design and run multi-week curricula and one-off workshops, mostly on Claude Code and
      practical AI workflows. The recent four-week working group with Women in Tech UK ended with
      every participant deploying a live website they'd built in-session. I make the attendee
      hubs, run sheets, demo fallbacks and sandboxes myself, and I retro every event honestly:
      what landed, what died, what changes next time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The credibility behind the teaching is simple. I'm not a developer. History degree, sales
      career. If the methods I teach got me to a 14-agent system in three months, they'll work for
      the people in the room.
    </p>

    <h2>Building</h2>
    <p>
      My own stack is the standing demo: agents that brief my meetings, clean my CRM, build
      campaigns and analyse my calls, plus the event hubs and small tools I ship for my own life.
      Most of it is public on GitHub, because "go and look" beats "trust me".
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Case studies</h2>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      {work.map((entry) => <WorkCard entry={entry} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="subscribe">
    <h2>Want a session like this for your team or community?</h2>
    <p>
      I run workshops, working groups and talks in London and remotely. Tell me the audience and
      the outcome you want; I'll suggest a format.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="mailto:jai.kharbanda@gmail.com?subject=Workshop%20enquiry">Invite me to run a session</a>
  </section>
</Base>
